    {
      "id": 106860,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-06-21T11:31:47.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I've never read the actual graphic novels, though I know they exist - I was in an unfortunately short-lived RPG over on RPOL a couple of years ago (RL stuff came up for the GM so he had to give that priority instead :() which is where pretty much all my knowledge of the Mouse Guard setting comes from. I have the PDF of the rulebook and I like the way the skills and stuff are done - pretty much all of char gen is aimed at getting your fluff sorted, with all your stats and skills plugging in in such a way that they enhance your character's backstory rather than just being numbers on a page or whatever. I wish I could have played my character longer - that's what frustrates me most about RPGs that fizzle after a short time (which pretty much every game I've ever played in has) - I spend all this time coming up with a character and her detailed backstory and stuff, but then can't take it anywhere because the game suddenly dies, and I'd've liked to have spent the time playing the character, levelling her up (well, Mouse Guard doesn't really have \"levels\" as such, but I'm speaking generally), developing her personality and all that.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
