      "raw": "<p>I&#39;ve never read the actual graphic novels, though I know they exist - I was in an unfortunately short-lived RPG over on RPOL a couple of years ago (RL stuff came up for the GM so he had to give that priority instead :() which is where pretty much all my knowledge of the Mouse Guard setting comes from. I have the PDF of the rulebook and I like the way the skills and stuff are done - pretty much all of char gen is aimed at getting your fluff sorted, with all your stats and skills plugging in in such a way that they enhance your character&#39;s backstory rather than just being numbers on a page or whatever. I wish I could have played my character longer - that&#39;s what frustrates me most about RPGs that fizzle after a short time (which pretty much every game I&#39;ve ever played in has) - I spend all this time coming up with a character and her detailed backstory and stuff, but then can&#39;t take it anywhere because the game suddenly dies, and I&#39;d&#39;ve liked to have spent the time playing the character, levelling her up (well, Mouse Guard doesn&#39;t really have &quot;levels&quot; as such, but I&#39;m speaking generally), developing her personality and all that.</p>",
